<article class="env-lemma" id="06AA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06AA">Lemma <span data-tag="06AA">29.35.17</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be an immersion of schemes over $S$. Assume that $Z$ is smooth over $S$. Then the canonical exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \to i^*\Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{Z/S} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/01UZ" data-tag="01UZ">29.33.15</a> is short exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The algebraic version of this lemma is the following: Given ring maps $A \to B \to C$ with $A \to C$ smooth and $B \to C$ surjective with kernel $J$, then the sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to J/J^2 \to C \otimes _ B \Omega _{B/A} \to \Omega _{C/A} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RU" data-tag="00RU">10.131.9</a> is exact. This is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06A8" data-tag="06A8">10.139.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>